pullRequests.body:
Creates stabilized Web Mode directly from the current Alpha 6 stabilized candidate.

Current head: `bc0cb5fbc5468887eefcd40c3c766ee2d64a3eca`.

Included:
- browser model aligned with desktop first-week, relationship, Home and episode rules;
- parity tests against the actual desktop engine;
- onboarding handoff pause/resume parity;
- browser-local Focus timer and Quiet mode;
- continuity delivery consumed only when delivery is still allowed;
- browser-local remembered-file metadata and Home materialization;
- self-contained embedded character assets;
- Playwright Chromium acceptance spec;
- self-contained Web Mode artifact packaging;
- static-host security config under `web-preview/vercel.json`.

Direct live-branch validation from the connected GitHub source confirms:
- `app.js` and `model.js` parse;
- all 42 runtime DOM ids exist;
- required character assets are present;
- no fetch/XMLHttpRequest/WebSocket/FileReader/arrayBuffer calls exist in the browser runtime;
- first-week choice, relationship score/stage, room props, Home scenes and one-stage-per-day plant progression match the desktop engine in executed parity checks.

GitHub Actions note: current CI/Test Builds/Web Mode E2E runs are failing before any executable step starts; connector metadata reports `steps=null` for every job. Do not interpret those runs as source-test failures or PASS evidence. Real Chromium E2E remains pending until a runner actually starts.

Full status: `docs/WEB_MODE_2026-09-21.md`.

Old prototype PR #16 is closed as superseded.

Next operational step: deploy `web-preview/` as a static HTTPS site. No backend is required. Keep this PR draft until real browser E2E and public URL smoke testing are completed.
